# UI test: a borrowed parameter on a `tool` (SC0192).
#
# §2.4 item 3: there is no caller to borrow from. Every argument was built
# from what arrived a moment ago and the tool is the only owner there is.
#
# Both spellings appear, so the deleted span is pinned for each — `&`
# alone, and `&mut` as one pair. Two parameters are two
# mistakes and therefore two diagnostics; that is not a cascade, and the count
# is what this case checks.

## Count the rows of a table.
tool count_rows(rows: &Array[Int], scratch: &mut Int) -> Int:
    0
